  "derivation": "Derived from the JS lot-4 seal (seal.json SHA-256 538ad9c207c13e2d2dee665717a2efed49f171cd6daedc3f09aa7654d332e35b), case file SHA-256 3db848f14bac6f14df714012e682c7276ff2364ff5f1b8198699d48420fc2679, by parity-sync decision PS-06 (DESIGN \u00a79.4 L723: IO object centres on one row line; RH = max(minHeight, max(object.h + label.h) + 2\u00b7padding), A = max(object.h/2), B = max(object.h/2 + label.h), cy = body.y + max(A, (RH + A \u2212 B)/2), object y = cy \u2212 h/2, one roundEven per coordinate): side row on Z-page (padding 8, minHeight 40): Task_A (a-first, 100000x80000, no label) and Task_B (z-last, 100000x80000, label height 14000); RH = max(40, 94000 + 2\u00b78) = 94016, A = 40000, B = 54000, cy = 0 + max(40000, (94016 + 40000 \u2212 54000)/2) = 40008; Task_A y = 40008 \u2212 40000 = 8 (per-block centring gave 7008); Task_B y 8 and label y 80008 unchanged; body height max(100000, 94016, 94008) = 100000 unchanged; the A-page row holds Task_B only (unchanged); Task_A has no incident edge and the page bounds do not change. The JS seal carries the decided values. Values owned by that seal (harmonization \u00a73; parity sync PS-H17). JS derivation: Explicitly bound grid successor: Task_A anchors on Y-consumer (opposite end Task_B, centre 350000) at left 300000; Task_B anchors on A-producer (Task_A centre 150000) but collides and moves to 400008; Lane_side grows to 500016. Row height 94016: Task_A y 7008, Task_B y 8, label (430008, 80008). On A-page Task_A is absent, so Task_B has no anchor and starts at 8. The theme's side-stripe declaration emits one record per represented page; its glyph is a header-band template without stripeWidth, so the stripe spans the whole grown region (harmonization K8): Z-page (0, 0, 500016, 100000), A-page (0, 0, 400000, 100000), label Auxiliary. Fails against: Using the base lane width for the stripe, a default stripe width, a stripe on one page only, or anchoring on an activity absent from the page.",
